$DATUM Chlorotrimethylsilane (0.270 mL, 2.1 mmol, 0.05 equiv) was added to a
mixture of (S)-4-amino-2-hydroxybutanoic acid 1 (5.00g, 42.0 mmol),
xylene (100 mL), and HMDS (61.5 mL, 294 mmol, 7.0 equiv) at rt. The
reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 12 h, cooled to rt, and diluted
with absolute ethanol (200 mL). The solvents were removed under reduced
pressure. Lactam 23 (7.30 g, quant recovery) as a tan solid, which was
used without further purification.
